course: dictionary
lesson: 9773
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «Surfing is a famous sport in Australia» means riding waves on a surfboard. «Surfing the web» means going from site to site on the internet, and the word web is your clue.
explain: Read the words around the word first. In «Shoulder surfing means watching someone type their PIN», surfing has nothing to do with waves. The clues are watching and PIN, so it means secretly watching over someone's shoulder.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If it does not make sense, try the next meaning. A dictionary lists all the meanings, so you can check which one fits.
fact: Surfing (noun) is the sport of riding on waves on a surfboard.
fact: «Web surfing» and «internet surfing» mean looking around on the internet, going from site to site.
fact: «Bodysurfing» and «crowd-surfing» mean riding or moving along without a surfboard, or on something else.
fact: «Shoulder surfing» means watching someone type their PIN.
fact: A «tsunami» is not one giant surfing wave: it is a series of huge waves made when the sea floor suddenly jerks up or down in an undersea earthquake.
exercise: «Surfing is a famous sport in Australia and Hawaii.» What does surfing mean here? | Hiding from a lifeguard | Looking around on the internet | *Riding waves on a surfboard
exercise: Maya says, «I spent all evening surfing the web.» What does surfing mean? | Lying on a board in the sea | Riding big waves at the beach | *Going from site to site on the internet
exercise: «Shoulder surfing means watching someone type their PIN.» What is the best meaning of shoulder surfing? | Swimming out past the waves | Telling a friend your password | *Secretly watching someone type their PIN | Carrying a surfboard on your shoulder
test: Which meaning of surfing fits «a surfing competition on the beach»? | Watching someone type their PIN | Going from site to site on the internet | *Riding waves on a surfboard in a contest
test: In «A tsunami is not one giant surfing wave», what is the writer saying? | *A tsunami is not a surfing wave; it is a series of huge waves | A tsunami is a small wave that is safe to ride | A tsunami is a famous surfing sport
exam: Which sentence uses «surfing» to mean looking around the internet? | Ben went surfing in Cornwall with his lifeguard | Lia said the surfing competition was cancelled | Tom took surfing lessons on Saturday | *Mia spent the afternoon surfing the web
